WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.094
Here is the boundary to remember.

2
00:00:02.094 --> 00:00:05.519
The name does not list the implemented ISA extensions.

3
00:00:05.519 --> 00:00:13.577
It does not prove privilege modes, cache organization, M M U or P M P support, issue width, verification coverage, or maturity.

4
00:00:13.577 --> 00:00:17.700
Even the six in CVA6 is a pipeline clue, not a performance score.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.854
The name is excellent for navigation: it narrows the family, width, class, or pipeline direction.

6
00:00:23.854 --> 00:00:31.150
Engineering conclusions begin only after the configuration table, design documentation, and release evidence agree.

